## Install

1. Download `{{APK}}` on the phone (or send it there).
2. Open it. Android asks to allow installing apps from that source (Settings, Apps, Special access,
   Install unknown apps): allow it for the app you opened the file from.
3. Google Play Protect may warn that the app is from an unknown developer: choose "Install anyway".
4. Open Openlive and add your server with the invite link its admin gave you.

Updates install over the old version (same signing key) and keep your data.

### Obtainium

[Obtainium](https://obtainium.imranr.dev/) can install and update the app from this page:

- App source URL: `https://github.com/henriquefps/openlive`
- Turn on "Include prereleases" (the beta is a pre-release).
- "Filter APKs by regular expression": `android`
- "Filter release titles by regular expression": `^Openlive Android` (the repository also has
  helper releases, which have no APK)

## Check the file

SHA-256 of the APK:

```text
{{APK_SHA}}  {{APK}}
```

`SHA256SUMS` has the same line (`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`). To check the signature (Android SDK
build-tools, `apksigner verify --print-certs {{APK}}`), the certificate SHA-256 must be:

```text
{{CERT}}
```
